        "execSummary":  "Stack Overflow\u0027s trust-scoring layer for AI agent knowledge consumption addresses one of the most underappreciated enterprise AI risks: agents confidently acting on outdated, unvalidated, or low-provenance internal knowledge. For customer support and operations leaders deploying agents at scale, the ability to score and gate knowledge by recency and expert validation is a prerequisite for reliable autonomous action—not a nice-to-have. The Slack and Teams integrations lower the barrier to connecting conversational knowledge sources, but also expand the attack surface for knowledge poisoning if input validation is weak. This positions Stack Internal as infrastructure-layer tooling that sits beneath agent orchestration platforms, which means procurement decisions about knowledge management now have direct implications for agent reliability.",
