        "summary":  "AWS introduces the Adjudicated Query design pattern for conducting large-scale compliance audits across thousands of leases using Amazon Quick and Bedrock. The architecture uses a conversational AI interface strictly for query translation and result narration, while a deterministic rules engine makes all actual compliance decisions—ensuring full auditability via a \u0027completeness receipt\u0027 that proves every record was evaluated. The system uses Amazon Aurora Serverless v2, Lambda-hosted MCP servers, and QuickSight for visualization, with six bounded operations preventing silent data narrowing.",
        "execSummary":  "Enterprises running large-scale document compliance reviews can now deploy an AI-augmented architecture that preserves full legal defensibility by ensuring AI never makes compliance decisions. The Adjudicated Query pattern is decision-relevant because it addresses the core enterprise governance concern: AI can assist at scale without becoming a liability in audit or regulatory scrutiny. The \u0027completeness receipt\u0027 invariant is a practical innovation for any organization that must demonstrate to regulators that no records were silently excluded. Leaders evaluating AI for legal, lease, or contract compliance workflows should examine this pattern as a governance-safe framework before approving autonomous AI decision-making in those domains.",
