        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Author Dan Roberts presents an evolved leadership framework of seven competencies—Coherence, Communication, Currency, Confidence, Conviction, Courage, and Change—required for technology executives navigating AI-driven disruption. The framework extends his original \u00277 Cs of Great Leaders\u0027 to address the accelerating pace of change AI demands, with each competency illustrated through examples of accomplished CIOs.",
        "execSummary":  "As AI reshapes technology leadership expectations, this framework offers senior IT leaders a practical self-assessment lens for the capabilities now required—particularly \u0027Currency\u0027 (continuous learning relevance) and \u0027Conviction\u0027 (decisive judgment with incomplete data), both directly tested by rapid AI adoption cycles. The decision-relevant insight is that technical AI fluency alone is insufficient; leaders who cannot communicate across organizational layers or act with courage under uncertainty will stall enterprise AI programs. For customer-support and operations leaders, \u0027Coherence\u0027—transforming organizational confusion into aligned movement—is especially critical as AI changes team structures and role definitions. The caveat is that the framework is prescriptive rather than empirical; leaders should treat it as a reflection tool rather than a validated diagnostic.",
