        "execSummary":  "Enterprise leaders evaluating agentic AI platforms now have a critical new option: IBM\u0027s Bob platform supports self-hosted, private, and sovereign cloud deployment, directly addressing the governance and data-residency blockers that have slowed enterprise adoption. For organizations in regulated industries—financial services, healthcare, government—this removes the \u0027we can\u0027t send code to a public cloud\u0027 objection and opens the door to broader agentic automation. The caveat is that self-hosting shifts operational burden back to internal teams; the platform\u0027s value depends heavily on internal MLOps maturity. Watch for competitors to follow with similar deployment flexibility as enterprises demand infrastructure control as a baseline requirement.",
