        "execSummary":  "Nvidia\u0027s entry into agent governance signals that the industry recognizes uncontrolled agent sprawl as an infrastructure-level risk, not just an application concern. By embedding safety controls—runtime sandboxing and continuous monitoring—at the chip and platform layer, Nvidia is positioning itself as the foundational layer for enterprise agentic AI, which has significant vendor-lock implications. For enterprise leaders, this raises a strategic question: govern agents at the infrastructure layer (Nvidia\u0027s bet) or at the orchestration layer (where most current tooling lives). The key caveat: analysts see no single governance solution winning, so a multi-layer governance strategy remains the prudent approach.",
