        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "According to New Relic\u0027s 2026 Observability Forecast, one-quarter of AI agents operate without any monitoring in enterprise settings, creating operational risk as autonomous systems modify code and infrastructure. This visibility gap is driving 80% of organizations to plan deployment of AI-specific observability solutions within twelve months. CIOs are increasingly turning to specialized observability platforms to track agent performance and ensure alignment with business objectives.",
        "execSummary":  "One in four enterprise AI agents running without monitoring is not a data point—it is an operational liability, particularly in customer-facing environments where an unmonitored agent can silently degrade experience or generate compliance exposure at scale. The 80% intent to deploy observability tools within a year signals that the market is catching up to the risk, but the window between now and deployment is where incidents will occur. For leaders responsible for AI-driven support or operations, the immediate action is an audit: catalog every deployed agent, confirm monitoring coverage, and establish escalation paths for anomalous behavior. The caveat is that observability tooling itself is fragmenting, so selecting platforms with cross-agent visibility—not just per-agent logging—is critical.",
