        "summary":  "Public opinion on AI is souring—majorities express nervousness and oppose AI infrastructure expansion—yet adoption continues to surge, with ChatGPT reaching a billion monthly users. The author argues that people\u0027s discontent stems not from the technology itself but from aggressive corporate promotion strategies and overhyped claims about AI\u0027s transformative power. The paradox reveals a complex relationship between public skepticism and private utility.",
